******************************************************************************** EasyMount.aii* by Dave Lyons  7-Jun-91** Copyright 1991-1993 Apple Computer, Inc* All Rights Reserved** Core code borrowed from "init.aii" in the QuickMount/Choose project,* originally by TGH (Tim Harrington) 04/06/88.********************************************************************************* 7..10-Jun-91 DAL 1.0d1*   Pretty much works.  You can double-click on existing QuickMount documents*     to mount servers.*   You can select one or more mounted servers and choose "Create Server Alias..."*     from the Finder's Extras menu.*   Holding down Option while double-clicking or Opening a QuickMount document*     forces the "Connect as" dialog up even if the password is okay or the*     document is set for Guest access.** 10..11-Jun-91 DAL --> 1.0d2*   Improved the Connect As dialog--comes up right for Guest access, etc.*   Fixed User ID fed to AcceptRequests (was garbage).*   Changed AcceptRequests string to "Apple~EasyMount~".** 23-Jun-91 DAL --> 1.0d3*   Changed UAM error message at Mark Day's suggestion.*   Added AlertWindow errors for "This icon isn't a server" and "You must*     first select one or more server icons."*   Now accepts request $8000 (srqMountServer) to mount a server volume.** 14-Jul-91 DAL --> 1.0d4*   Now informs the Finder that the directory changed when you create a*     new alias file.*   Now enables and disables the Extras menu item as appropriate (when the*     selection changes).** 30-Jul-91 DAL --> 1.0d5*   Extras menu item is now initially disabled.** 5-Aug-91 DAL*   Check for AppleShare FST presence; if it ain't there, set the "unload*   me" flag on the stack, so the system will unload me.** 19-Aug-91 DAL --> 1.0d6*   Andy added a dc.w 0 to the add-to-extras result buffer, to go with*     Finder 6.0d46.  I moved it by one line to be in the right place.'** 4-Sep-91 DAL --> 1.0d7*   Turned on flag bit in menu item, so the Finder knows it's our first*     item (this creates a dividing line above our item if we are not*     the first thing in the Extras menu).** 24-Oct-91 MSD --> 1.0d8*   ¥ I noticed TryMount was doing asynchronous NBP lookup.  I can't figure*     out why (the code waits until it completes anyway), so I simplified it*     by making the lookup synchronous.*   ¥ If volume didn't get mounted, you no longer get logged off if you were*     already logged on.*   ¥ The user volume in the FIMountVol flags is now set correctly.  If the*     volume couldn't be found in the FPGetSrvrInfo reply, the user volume*     flag will not be set.*   ¥ When asked for a password, the Guest radio button is now dimmed if*     guests do not have access to the server.* 29-Oct-91 MSD (still 1.0d8)*   ¥ When you open a document with the Option key down, and you're already*     logged on, you shouldn't get the Connect As dialog (it's not worth*     fixing the dialog to show who you've logged on as).** 31-Oct-91 MSD --> 1.0d9*   ¥ Changed the error messages so they are each a template and allow string*     substitution (it used to use one error template and subtitute the body*     of the message.)  Changed the text of the server not found message to*     include the name of the volume.*  1-Nov-91 MSD*   ¥ TestUserVolume wasn't advancing its pointer to the next volume name*     properly, so it wouldn't identify a user volume that wasn't the first*     volume returned in the list.*   ¥ Changed structure of dialog/mount loop so it can try first without displaying*     an error.  Then it falls into the loop where it displays a message for*     any error (including bad password).*   ¥ The indices used to access the error tables in ReportMountError were off*     by two bytes (which meant the unknown error case never worked right).** 3-Nov-91 DAL*   Changed several exclamation marks to periods in error messages...they were*     getting on my nerves.*   When a volume is successfully mounted, and on error $0A11 (volume already*     mounted), we now try asking the Finder to open the window (or bring it to*     the front), unless the Control key is down.  This is done with a kludgey*     Run Queue task for the moment, since I have to let the Finder finish*     mounting the server before I can successfully ask the Finder to open its*     window.**  8-Nov-91 MSD --> 1.0d10*   ¥ After a volume is mounted, it now calls the AppleShare FST's FST_Specific*     call Get_User_Path to force FIUserPrefix to be set.** 18-Nov-91 DAL --> 1.0d11*   ¥ To open windows faster, force a ScanDevices and kill the 2-second delay.** 24-Nov-91 DAL --> 1.0d12*   ¥ Use finderSaysIdle to know when it's safe to open the window for a volume*     we mounted.** 25-Nov-91 DAL*   ¥ Under pre-6.0, init now asks to be unloaded.*   ¥ On finderSaysBeforeOpen, we now check whether this is an Open or*     a Print.  We only respond to Open.** 8-Jan-92 DAL*   ¥ Accept systemSaysEjectingDev to kill the need-to-open-window flag.** 28-Jan-92 DAL 1.0d15*   ¥ Make theUserName buffer longer (avoid putting a garbage byte into the*     data files).**   NOTE:  EasyMount does not support 32-character user names; max is 31.********************************************************************************* 24-Feb-92 DAL, 1.1d1 for 6.0.1** Changed tellFinderXXX calls to set the SendRequest stopAfterOne bit.  This* is slightly more efficient.** 25-Feb-92 DAL** On handling a redundant finderSaysGoodbye call, we take no action.* We now accept srqGoAway.** 04-Mar-92 DMA** Adding support for opening folders, documents, and applications on any * device.** 13-Mar-92 DAL --> 1.1d2** Minor stuff on top of Darin's stuff:  Changed "Create Alias..." to* "Make Alias..." and cleaned up a couple of comments.  Added a note* at handleEjectingDev that this will need to be fixed up.** 17-Mar-92 DMA --> 1.1d3** Fix so offline volumes will be mounted and displayed before attempting* to open windows, apps, or documents from them.  Old style EasyMount* documents now correctly open the server volume window.** 25-Mar-92 DAL** Updated messages to say "disk" instead of "volume", and not to use* "mount."** 15-Jul-92 DAL --> 1.1d7 for 6.0.1d7** Crunched code by using OpenResourceFileByID, HiliteCtlByID, SetCtlValueByID.** 17-Jul-92 DAL --> 1.1d8 for 6.0.1d8** Turned on mwUpdateAll bit in DoModalWindow call.* Changed "server is shutting down, so you can't log on" to say that it might* be starting up, instead.** 12-Aug-92 DAL --> 1.1d9 for 6.0.1d9** EasyMount loads even if network is not available, since it's useful for* local networks now.** 25-Aug-92 DAL --> 1.1d10 for 6.0.1d10** Changed the AppleTalk-busy message to suggest closing network control panels.** 15-Sep-92 DAL --> 1.1d11 for 6.0.1d11** Fixed bad-password message to match the AppleShare control panel.** 17-Sep-92 DAL** Added check for zero volumes in TestUserVolume.** 26-Jan-93 JCM --> 1.1d13 for 6.0.1d13** ¥ Fixed "Save" from the connect-as dialog to not destroy EasyMount 1.0 documents.*   Now, we never re-write the alias pathaname, since there never was a mechanism to*   change an aliases target after it was created. This puts to rest the parameter out*   of range error many reported.** ¥ Made srqMountServer work properly with the new 1.1 file format that includes the*   alias pathname at the end. In the process, I re-worked most of the file read code*   to actually report errors properly if any occurred. Previously, errors would have*   been detected after a few GS/OS calls, but the error code would not be passed back*   up the calling chain.**  2-Mar-93 JCM --> 1.1d14 for 6.0.1.d14** ¥ Made this thing work in 320 mode. I moved the controls around a bit and hid the*   window when it's initially created.** ¥ Removed some dead code from TryMount which was around from when we didn't use the*   linked-list and had a single pathname buffer to mount.** ¥ Made the "don't open windows when control key is down" feature work again.** 16-Mar-93 JCM ** ¥ Added Dave's two new calls, UseColorTable and RestoreColorTable, to the password*   dialog. This makes our icon look cool, even in 320-mode, since we ask for the*   standard 640-mode color table.** ¥ Fixed the password dialog to not ask Finder to open a window when you clicked*   "Cancel". I moved the calls to AddToPathList from ParseFile to MountByData.*   Before, we would always ask the window to be opened, even if the user cancelled*   the mount, or we got an error.** ¥ If you ever went through the password dialog with an 8-character password, but*   made no changes to it, it would be truncated to 7 chars and you then couldn't*   connect since it would now be wrong.** 18-Mar-93 JCM** ¥ Fixed the "don't open windows when control key is down" feature work again, for the*   second time. I fixed it to read the modifiers that Finder fed us, but I masked for*   the control key with the hardware modifiers bit mask, not the event control key mask.*   I now do it the right way.** 19-Mar-93 JCM** ¥ One more fix to the "don't open windows when control key is down" feature. We were*   calling AddToPath list regardless of the state of the control key. In the case where*   you had previously mounted a server volume but let the window open, we would add that*   disposed handle to the path list. Finder doesn't like that too much, and neither do I.** 23-Mar-93 DAL** Added 4 lines in the request procedure to make it reentrant.  Maybe I'm just being* paranoid, or maybe not.  (The pitfall avoided is an interrupt-time SendRequest* coming through and making our original dispatch use the wrong request code.)** 23-Mar-93 JCM/DAL** ¥ Fixed two of Dave's four lines to be in the right place. He was pulling and saving*   a value after the data bank had been restored, which resulted in it being put into*   the wrong bank most of the time.** ¥ Now calling GetNextEvent right after we show the password window so we can eat any*   possible system window deactivates. This allows us to safely nest UseColorTable and*   RestoreColorTable without worrying about the screen being restored by someone else.** 25-Mar-93 SS** ¥ Added menu key equivalents 'Mm'.** 25-Mar-93 JCM** ¥ Made local aliases work again. We were never telling Finder to open them if the*   document had a pcount of 1. Whoops.** ¥ Now we only allow aliases to be made for disks, folders, and applications.** 2-Apr-93 JCM** ¥ Fixed srvNameBuff and zoneNameBuf to be large enough to hold 31-char GS/OS strings.*   They were large enough to hold 32-char PStrings, but that's not what the FST returns.********************************************************************************* ============* Things to do* ============** Investigate extending the EasyMount document format to locate specific*   folders (or files?) on a server.  (Or even locally?)** Should not allow password to be left lying around in memory.** Should encrypt passwords at least a little (in files).** When you click on Registered User and there's no name, it should default*   to the ATINIT name.** Should prompt for volume password if it isn't recorded.*******************************************************************************	print push,off	include 'all.macros'	include 'e16.finder'	include 'e16.gsos'	include 'e16.locator'	include 'e16.quickdraw'	print popRamDispatch	equ $E11014True	equ $8000False	equ $0000********************************************************************************* SendRequest codes that we accept (other than finderSays codes, in E16.Finder,* and system-wide calls, in E16.Locator)********************************************************************************srqMountServer	equ $8000********************************************************************************* Structure of the finderSaysBeforeOpen parm block********************************************************************************opCount	equ 0oPathname	equ opCount+2oSmallRect	equ oPathname+4oFiletype	equ oSmallRect+4oAuxtype	equ oFiletype+2oModifiers	equ oAuxtype+4	;for Finder 6.0d39oReserved	equ oModifiers+2oPrintFlag	equ oReserved+4	;for Finder 6.0d59********************************************************************************* Filetype information we care about********************************************************************************QuickMountFileType	equ $00E2QuickMountAuxtype	equ $ffff************************************************************************************************************************************************************EasyMount	procname	import DES	Case off	sta >myMemID	pha	_QDVersion	pla	and #$0fff	cmp #$0307	bcc @unload	;25-Nov-91 DAL;;;	jsr CheckForAppleShare;;;	bcc @HaveAppleShare	bra @StayLoaded@unload	lda #1	;set the "unload me" flag	sta 4,s	rtl;;;@HaveAppleShare@StayLoaded	pushlong #myReqProcName	lda >myMemID	pha	;memory ID	pushlong #myReqProc	_AcceptRequests	bcc @ok	_SysBeep@ok	rtlmyReqProcName	str 'Apple~EasyMount~'myMemID	dc.w 0;**************************************************************;*;* CheckForAppleShare -- return CLC if the AppleShare FST is here;*;**************************************************************;CheckForAppleShare	pushlong #fstSpecificParms;	pea $2033	;FSTSpecific;	jsl $e100b0;	bcc @ok;	cmp #$53;	beq @ok;	sec;	rts;@ok	clc;	rts;;fstSpecificParms	dc.w 2	;pCount = 2;	dc.w $000D	;FST ID = AppleShare;	dc.w 0	;illegal FST-specific code**************************************************************** myReqProc -- look for finderSaysBeforeOpen with a*              QuickMount document***************************************************************myReqProc	nameoldDPage	equ 1RTL1	equ oldDPage+2DataOut	equ RTL1+3DataIn	equ DataOut+4Request	equ DataIn+4Result	equ Request+2		phd	tsc	tcd		phb	phk	plb*** added 23-Mar-93 DAL to make the request proc reentrant (paranoia?)	lda requestTable	pha*** end 23-Mar-93	lda <Request	sta requestTable	ldx #requestTableEnd-requestTable@search	dex	dex	dex	dex	cmp requestTable,x	bne @search	jsr (requestTable+2,x)	;return SEC = handled	ror <Result*** added 23-Mar-93 DAL	pla	sta requestTable*** end 23-Mar-93	plb	pld	lda 2,s	sta 12,s	lda 1,s	sta 11,s	ply	ply	ply	ply	ply	rtlrequestTable	dc.w $7777,ignoreRequest	dc.w srqGoAway,handleGoAway	;added 25-Feb-92 DAL	dc.w finderSaysExtrasChosen,handleExtrasChosen	dc.w systemSaysEjectingDev,handleEjectingDev	dc.w finderSaysBeforeOpen,handleOpenFailed	dc.w finderSaysSelectionChanged,handleSelectionChanged	dc.w finderSaysHello,handleHello	dc.w finderSaysGoodbye,handleGoodbye	dc.w srqMountServer,handleMountServer	dc.w finderSaysIdle,handleFinderIdlerequestTableEndignoreRequest	clc	rts********************************************************************************* handleGoAway** Respond to an srqGoAway request by saying Yes, we can go away (accept* the request and return our userID in the dataOut buffer).** dataOut:*   +000: recvCount*   +002: userID (return 0 if we cannot go away)*   +004: flags (0 = not restartable from RAM, $8000 = restartable)********************************************************************************handleGoAway	name	lda myMemID	ldy #2	sta [<dataOut],y	;userID = my ID	iny	iny	lda #0	sta [<dataOut],y	;flags = 0	sec	;accept the request	rts********************************************************************************* handleHello********************************************************************************handleHello	name	pea tellFinderAddToExtras	pea sendToName+stopAfterOne	;24-Feb-92 DAL	pushlong #nameOfFinder	pushlong #aliasItemTemplate	pushlong #addToExtrasBuffer	_SendRequest	sec	;handled	rtsnameOfFinder	str 'Apple~Finder~'aliasItemTemplate	dc.w $8000	;version (bit 15 = dividing line flag for Finder)	dc.w 0	;id (ignored)	dc.b 'Mm'	;key equivs  *** added 25-Mar-93 SS	dc.w 0	;check character	dc.w $0080	;item flag (disabled)	dc.l myAliasItemNamemyAliasItemName	str 'Make Alias...'addToExtrasBuffer	dc.w 0	dc.w 0makeAliasItemID	dc.w 0	dc.w 0	;this is result space for the Extras Menu ID********************************************************************************* handleGoodbye********************************************************************************handleGoodbye	name*** added 25-Feb-92 DAL -- No action on a redundant finderSaysGoodbye	lda makeAliasItemID	beq @doNothing*** end 25-Feb-92	pea tellFinderRemoveFromExtras	pea sendToName+stopAfterOne	;24-Feb-92 DAL	pushlong #nameOfFinder	pea 0	lda makeAliasItemID	pha	pushlong #removeFromExtrasBuffer	_SendRequest	stz makeAliasItemID@doNothing	sec	;handled	rtsremoveFromExtrasBuffer dc.w 0,0********************************************************************************* handleSelectionChanged** Get the current selection and see if we should enable or disable our* menu item in the Extras menu.********************************************************************************handleSelectionChanged name*** added 25-Feb-92 DAL -- If we have no menu item, don't mess with it (moved check)	lda makeAliasItemID	beq @noAction*** end 25-Feb-92	jsr GetSelectedIcons	bcs @disable	lda iconsResult	bne @disable	;error getting icons		pushlong iconsHandle	jsr CheckTheIcons	bcs @disable@enable	ldx #$300F	;EnableMItem	bra @set@disable	ldx #$310F	;DisableMItem@set	lda makeAliasItemID	pha	jsl $e10000	;X already = function	jsr DispIconsHndl@noAction	sec	;handled	rts********************************************************************************* CheckTheIcons** Return CLC if we should enable our Make Alias item, based on* the selected icons.** Input: String handle on stack** Format of string handle is:*   +000 WORD  number of strings*   +002 WSTR  first string*   +xxx WSTR  second string*    ...** Output:  carry flag********************************************************************************CheckTheIcons	name	phd	pha	pha	;ptr	tsc	tcd@ptr	equ 1@oldD	equ @ptr+4@rts	equ @oldD+2@handle	equ @rts+2	pei <@handle+2	pei <@handle	_HLock	ldy #2	lda [<@handle],y	sta <@ptr+2	lda [<@handle]	sta <@ptr	lda [<@ptr]	;Get the number of selected items	sec	;Assume no icons (carry set)	beq @done	;and leave	clc	;Icons are selected, return carry clear@done	pla	pla	;ptr	pld	plx	pla	pla	phx	rts********************************************************************************* handleExtrasChosen********************************************************************************handleExtrasChosen	name	lda <dataIn	cmp makeAliasItemID	beq @makeAlias	clc	;did not handle	rts@makeAlias	jsr GetSelectedIcons	bcs @ouch	lda iconsResult	bne @ouch	jsr GetStandardFile	bcs @ouch	pushlong IconsHandle	jsr MakeTheAliases	jsr KillStandardFile	sec	;handled@exit	jsr DispIconsHndl	rts@ouch	_SysBeep	clc	bra @exitgetIconsBuffer	dc.w 0	;recvCounticonsResult	dc.w 0	;finderResulticonsLocation	dc.l 0	;0=desktop, <>0=window pointericonsHandle	dc.l 0	;StringHandle of selected iconsGetSelectedIcons	name	stz iconsHandle+1	pea tellFinderGetSelectedIcons	pea sendToName+stopAfterOne	;24-Feb-92 DAL	pushlong #nameOfFinder	pea 0	pea 0	;dataIn = reserved	pushlong #getIconsBuffer	_SendRequest	rtsDispIconsHndl	name	php	lda iconsHandle+1	beq @noHandle	pushlong iconsHandle	_DisposeHandle@noHandle	plp	rts********************************************************************************* MakeTheAliases** For each server, use SFPutFile to ask the user where to put a QuickMount* document to mount it, and create the document.** Input: String handle on stack** Format of string handle is:*   +000 WORD  number of strings*   +002 WSTR  first string*   +xxx WSTR  second string*    ...** Output:  none (parameter is stripped)********************************************************************************MakeTheAliases	name	phd	pha	;numStrings	pha	pha	;ptr	tsc	tcd@ptr	equ 1@numStrings	equ @ptr+4@oldD	equ @numStrings+2@rts	equ @oldD+2@handle	equ @rts+2	pei <@handle+2	pei <@handle	_HLock	ldy #2	lda [<@handle],y	sta <@ptr+2	lda [<@handle]	sta <@ptr	lda [<@ptr]	sta <@numStrings	beq @oopsNoIcons	lda #2	jsr @addToPtr@repeat	jsr @MakeOneAlias	bcs @done	lda [<@ptr]	;bump ptr by length+2	inc a	inc a	jsr @addtoPtr	dec <@numStrings	bne @repeat@done	pla	pla	;ptr	pla	;numStrings	pld	plx	pla	pla	phx	rts@addToPtr	clc	adc <@ptr	sta <@ptr	bcc @1	inc <@ptr+2@1	rts@oopsNoIcons	pea $400C	;operation failed	_SysBeep2	pha	;space for button	pea $0020	pea 0	pea 0	;no substitutions	pushlong #noIconsMessage	_AlertWindow	pla	;button # (ignore)	bra @done********************************************************************************* @makeOneAlias -- make a QuickMount document** Input: <@ptr is a WString pathname of a mounted server volume** Output:  CLC = Created an alias file where the user wanted*          SEC = stop (error or cancel)********************************************************************************@makeOneAlias	ldy <@ptr+2	lda <@ptr	clc	adc #2	bcc @3	iny@3	sty FullPathPtr+2	;Save ptr to the pathname	sta FullPathPtr*** Added - 25-Mar-93 JCM - Only allow aliases for disks, folders, and apps.	ldy <@ptr+2	lda <@ptr		jsr GetFileInfo	;see if we can deal with this type	bcs @badType	jsr ValidateType		bcc @typeOk@badType	pha	;space for AlertWindow result	pea $0021	;flags (cool button layout + substitute pStrings)	lda #0	pha	pha	;no sub strings	pea ErrNope>>16	;push high word of error message pointer	pea ErrNope	;push low word of message pointer	_AlertWindow	;show the alert	pla	;ignore the button pressed	clc		rts@typeOk*** End - 25-Mar-93 JCM	lda <@ptr+2	ldy <@ptr	jsr GetServerInfo	lda #2	;Flag it as a server	bcc @IsAServer	dec a	;Unless we find out its not@IsAServer	sta AliasPCount		lda [<@ptr]	;Get the path length	sta AliasPathSize	sta FullPathLen 	;And save it; Copy the name for standard file.  If it's a pathname with colons, just ; copy the filename.@continue	stz defaultName	;Clear length word	sep #$30	;of destination	longa off	longi off		ldy FullPathLen	;Get length of string	beq @ZeroLength	@BackupLoop	lda [<@ptr],y	;Is the char a colon?	cmp #':'	beq @FarEnough	;Yes, start copying	dey	;Backup a char	bne @BackupLoop	;If not beginning, go again	iny	;Up past length word	@FarEnough	ldx #0	;X contains length of new string@CopyLoop	iny	;Forward one char	lda [<@ptr],y	;Copy the char	sta defaultName+2,x	inx	cpy FullPathLen	;Have we hit the end?	blt @CopyLoop	beq @CopyLoop	stx defaultName	;Store length@ZeroLength	rep #$30	;Back to long mode	longa on	longi on		pea 120	;x	pea 30	;y	pea 0	pushlong #sfPrompt	pea 0	pushlong #defaultName	pushlong #newReplyRec	_SFPutFile2	bcs @ouch	lda rrGood	beq @cancel	jsr WriteNewAliasFile	php	pha	pushlong rrNameRef	_DisposeHandle	pushlong rrPathRef	_DisposeHandle	pla	plp	bcs @ouch@exit	rts@ouch	jsr ShowErrorWindow@cancel	sec	rtsnoIconsMessage	dc.b '32/First select one or more icons./^#1',0ShowErrorWindow	name	pha	php	pha	;space for ErrorWindow result	ldx #0	phx	;subType	phx	phx	;subArray	pha	;error	_ErrorWindow	pla	;button number (ignore)		plp	pla	rtssfPrompt	str 'Create alias as:'defaultName	ds.b 36newReplyRecrrGood	dc.w 0rrFileType	dc.w 0rrAuxType	dc.l 0	dc.w 3	;name is new handlerrNameRef	dc.l 0	dc.w 3	;path is new handlerrPathRef	dc.l 0********************************************************************************* GetServerInfo** Input:  AY = pathname of server volume** Output: ReadBuffer is filled in (UserName, VolumeName, EntityName)*         SEC = error********************************************************************************GetServerInfo	name	phd	pha	phy	;keep path on stack (@volname)	tsc	tcd@volname	equ 1	jsr ZeroReadBuffer	; copy @volname (WString) into VolumeName (PString).  Only copies until the; the first colon (exclusive) and omits any leading colon.	ldy #2	;Skip first colon if there is one	sep #$30	longa off	longi off	stz VolumeName		lda [<@volname],y	cmp #':'	beq @SkipLeadingColon	sta VolumeName+1	;Not a colon, keep it	inc VolumeName@SkipLeadingColon	iny	@CopyVolLoop	tya	;Have we reached the end?	dec a	dec a	cmp [<@volname]	beq @DoneWithCopy	lda [<@volname],y	cmp #':'	;Leave if we hit another colon	beq @DoneWithCopy	tyx	;Save the character in the	ldy VolumeName	;appropriate place in the new	iny	;string.	sta VolumeName,y	sty VolumeName	txy	iny	bra @copyVolLoop	@DoneWithCopy	rep #$30	longa on	longi on** Get Server name and zone name*	lda <@volName+2	ldy <@volName	sta serverPath+2	sty serverPath	sta devNumPath+2	sty devNumPath	pushlong #GetSrvrNameParms	pea $2033	;FSTSpecific	jsl $e100b0	bcs @ouch** copy server name, 'AFPServer', zone name into EntityName*	lda theServerName	xba	sta theServerName	lda theZoneName	xba	sta theZoneName	ldx #0	;bumped along by AppendVolPString	ldy #^theServerName+1	lda #theServerName+1	jsr AppendVolPString	lda #CAFPName	ldy #^CAFPName	jsr AppendVolPString	ldy #^theZoneName+1	lda #theZoneName+1	jsr AppendVolPString*** get user name & stuff it into UserName	pushlong #GetDevNumParms	pea $2020	;GetDevNumber	jsl $e100b0	bcs @ouch	lda theDevNumber	sta userDevNumber	pushlong #UserInfoParms	pea $2033	;FSTSpecific	jsl $e100b0	bcs @ouch	lda theUserName	xba	sta theUserName	pushlong #theUserName+1	pushlong #UserName	pushlong #32	_BlockMove	clc	bra @exit@ouch	sec	and #$00ff@exit	plx	plx	pld	rtsGetSrvrNameParms	dc.w 5	;pcount	dc.w $000D	;AppleShare FST	dc.w $000D	;GetSrvrNameserverPath	dc.l 0	dc.l srvNameBuff	dc.l zoneNameBuff*** Fixed - 2-Apr-93 JCM - Allow 32-char names.;srvNameBuff	dc.w 34;theServerName	ds.b 32;;zoneNameBuff	dc.w 34;theZoneName	ds.b 32srvNameBuff	dc.w 36theServerName	ds.b 34zoneNameBuff	dc.w 36theZoneName	ds.b 34*** End - 2-Apr-93 JCMGetDevNumParms	dc.w 2	;pcountdevNumPath	dc.l 0theDevNumber	dc.w 0UserInfoParms	dc.w 4	;pcount	dc.w $000D	;AppleShare FST	dc.w $0006	;User InfouserDevNumber	dc.w 0	dc.l userNameBuff;userNameBuff	dc.w 34;theUserName	ds.b 32*** 28-Jan-92 DALuserNameBuff	dc.w 36theUserName	ds.b 34*** end 28-Jan-92** AppendVolPString** Input:  YA = pointer to pstring*          X = offset into EntityName structure** Output: Stored string, advanced X*AppendVolPString	name	phd	phy	pha	tsc	tcd	sep #$30	longa off	longi off	ldy #0@char	lda [1],y	sta EntityName,x	inx	iny	tya	cmp [1]	bcc @char	beq @char	rep #$30	longa on	longi on	ply	ply	pld	rts********************************************************************************* WriteNewAliasFile** Input:  contents of ReadBuffer must be valid*         rrPathRef -- handle to new alias file pathname********************************************************************************WriteNewAliasFile	NAME	;entry used by Standard File new-alias creation code	pushlong rrPathRef	_HLock	lda rrPathRef	ldx rrPathRef+2	jsr DerefPathname	;XA = rrPathRef^+2 (it's a result buffer!)	jsr SavePathPtrs	;save pointers to destination alias file pathname	bra WriteAliasCommon********************************************************************************* RewriteAliasFile - Used when "Save" is clicked in the server password dialog.** Input:  contents of ReadBuffer must be valid*         X (high)/ Acc (low) contain pointer to destination alias file pathname.********************************************************************************RewriteAliasFile	NAME	jsr SavePathPtrs	;save pointers to destination alias file pathname	stz FullPathPtr+1	;flag to not write the original file path at the endWriteAliasCommon	NAME	lda #3	;read/write	sta OpenAccess@openFile	_OpenGS OpenBlock	bcc @writeFile	;the file already exists, just rewrite the header		cmp #fileNotFound	bne @err	_CreateGS CreateBlock	bcc @openFile		bra @err@writeFile	lda OpenRef	sta ReadRef	sta CloseRef	sta FullPathRef	_WriteGS ReadBlock		;write the standard header	lda FullPathPtr+1		;are we re-writing a file? (changing pwd/user)	beq @isExistingFile		; yup, no need to write the path	_WriteGS FullPathBlock@isExistingFile	php	pha	_CloseGS CloseBlock	pla	plp@err	rtsDestroyBlock	dc.w 1	;pcountdestroyPath	dc.l 0CreateBlock	dc.w 4	;pcountcreatePath	dc.l 0	dc.w $00C3	;unlocked	dc.w QuickMountFileType	dc.l QuickMountAuxtypeDerefPathname	NAME	phd	phx	pha	tsc	tcd	ldy #2	lda [1],y	tax	lda [1]	clc	adc #2	bcc @1	inx@1	ply	ply	pld	rts	SavePathPtrs	NAME	stx destroyPath+2	sta destroyPath	stx createPath+2	sta createPath	stx fileNamePtr+2	;for Open	sta fileNamePtr	rts********************************************************************************* GetStandardFile -- if StdFile is not here, get it and start it up********************************************************************************sfToolNumber	equ $0017GetStandardFile	name	stz weStartedSF	pea 0	_SFStatus	pla	bne @done	pea sfToolNumber	pea 0	;minimum version	_LoadOneTool	bcs @oops	inc weStartedSF	pha	pha	;space for NewHandle	pea $0000	;size high	pea $0100	;size low	lda myMemID	pha	pea $C015	;attributes = fixed bank, etc.	ldx #0	phx	phx	;loc=0	_NewHandle	plx	ply	bcs @oops	stx sfHandle	sty sfHandle+2	phd	phy	phx	tsc	tcd	lda [1]	sta sfDirPage	plx	ply	pld	lda myMemID	pha	lda sfDirPage	pha	_SFStartUp	rts@oops	sec	rts@done	clc	rts********************************************************************************* KillStandardFile -- if we got StdFile ourselves, shut it back down********************************************************************************KillStandardFile	name	lda weStartedSF	beq @done	_SFShutDown	pea sfToolNumber	_UnloadOneTool	pushlong sfHandle	_DisposeHandle	stz weStartedSF@done	rtsweStartedSF	dc.w 0sfHandle	dc.l 0sfDirPage	dc.w 0**************************************************************************************************************************************************************** handleMountServer** dataIn points to:*   +000: data size (including this data word)*   +002: image of Server alias document (QM document)** dataOut points to:*   +000: receive count*   +002: error code********************************************************************************handleMountServer	NAME		jsr ZeroReadBuffer	lda <dataIn	ldx <dataIn+2		clc	adc #ReadBufferLen+2	bcc @saveSourcePtr		inx	@saveSourcePtr	sta ReadPathPtr	;pass pathname source ptr to ParseFile	stx ReadPathPtr+2		phx	pha	;source for BlockMove	pushlong #theDataLength  ;dest for BlockMove	pea 0	pea ReadBufferLen+2 ;size for BlockMove	_BlockMove	stz theModifiers	;mark Option key not down (1-Nov-91 MSD)	lda #0	;flag = file not on disk	jsr ParseFile	bcs @exitMountServer ;couldn't get a handle	jsr MountByData	lda TryMountError@exitMountServer	ldy #2	sta [<dataOut],y	;store error code in dataOut buffer	sec	;we handled it	rts**************************************************************************************************************************************************************** handleOpenFailed** The Finder wants us to open some documents, since it couldn't* find an application to launch.** If this one is a QuickMount document, let's try to mount a server!** DataIn points to the following structure:*   +000 WORD  parameter count (at least 7)*   +002 LONG  pointer to class-one pathname*   +006 LONG  pointer to rectangle to zoom from (NIL if none appropriate) *   +010 WORD  filetype*   +012 LONG  auxtype*   +016 WORD  modifiers*   +018 LONG  reserved (icon handle)*   +022 WORD  PrintFlag (0=Open, nonzero=Print)** Return with SEC if we handled it, CLC if we did not.********************************************************************************handleOpenFailed	name	*** added 25-Nov-91 DAL -- only honor Open, not Print	ldy #oPrintFlag	lda [<dataIn],y	bne @notOpen*** end 25-Nov-91	ldy #oFiletype	lda [<dataIn],y	;check filetype	cmp #QuickMountFileType	bne notQM	ldy #oAuxtype+2	lda [<dataIn],y	bne notQM	dey	dey	lda [<dataIn],y	;check auxiliary type	cmp #QuickMountAuxtype	beq handleQMdocument@notOpennotQM	clc	rts********************************************************************************* handleQMdocument** DataIn points to the following structure:*   +000 WORD  parameter count (at least 4)*   +002 LONG  pointer to class-one pathname*   +006 LONG  pointer to rectangle to zoom from (NIL if none appropriate) *   +010 WORD  filetype*   +012 LONG  auxtype********************************************************************************handleQMdocument	name	ldy #oModifiers	lda [<dataIn],y	sta theModifiers	pha	pha	_GetCursorAdr	pla	sta oldCursor	pla	sta oldCursor+2	_WaitCursor	ldy #oPathname+2	lda [<dataIn],y	tax	dey	dey	lda [<dataIn],y	jsr MountByDocument	;takes pathname in AX, returns error code in Carry/A		php	pha	pushlong oldCursor	_SetCursor	pla	plp	bcs failed		sec		rtsfailed	jsr ReportMountError		sec	;we handled it		rtsoldCursor	dc.l 0theModifiers	dc.w 0***************************************************************** MountByDocument** Input: Pathname pointer in X-Register high, Accumulator low** Output: SEC = error*         CLC = OK****************************************************************MountByDocument	NAME	stx theFilePath+2	sta theFilePath	tay	;get path low in Y like ReadData wants	jsr ReadData	;path in XY	bcc MountByData		rts** MountByData -- input = data in ReadBuffer*                output = CLC if no error, error in MountError*MountByData	lda AliasPCount	; Check if it's a server volume	beq @JustServerVol	;old-style server-only document	dec a	;is it a local thing?	beq justOpenWindow	; yup, just open that window	dec a	;new-style document?	beq @JustServerVol	; yup, deal with the server		rts	;file will be opened at next finderSaysIdle	@JustServerVol	jsr FindServer	;do NBP lookup first	bcs exitMountLoop	;couldn't find server		jsr AllocSPReply	; get room for ASP reply buffer	bcs exitMountLoop		jsr GetStatus	; see if guest login is enabled	bcs @dispose		lda theModifiers	and #$0800	; get Option key bit	beq @silent	; no Option key, try silently first	jsr TestLoggedOn	; are we logged on yet?	bcc @AskPassword	; no, so ask for a password first	; Try to mount silently first@silent	jsr TryMount	bcc mounted	cmp #$0A15	; bad password?	bne exitMountLoop	; no, don't bother asking; Mount didn't work or Option was down.  Ask for password@AskPassword	jsr PromptForPassword	bcc @TryAgain	;they clicked OK, so try again	lda #0	;was cancelled, don't display error	beq @dispose	;dispose of memory and return error@TryAgain	jsr TryMount	bcc mounted	; it worked this time!		cmp #$0A15	;bad password?	bne exitMountLoop	;other error, give up		sta TryMountError	; save error	jsr ReportMountError ; show error to user		bra @AskPassword	; let 'em try again	@dispose	pha	; save error		jsr FreeSPReply	; dispose of reply buffer		pla	; recover errorexitMountLoop	sta TryMountError	; save error number	sec	;volume was not mounted		rtsmounted; 8-Nov-91 MSD: Call the AppleShare FST's GetUserPath call for the; side-effect of setting FIUserPrefix (in case the first user volume; was mounted).	pushlong #GetUserPath	pea $2033	;FSTSpecific	jsl $e100b0	; call GS/OS; End 8-Nov-91 MSD	jsr FreeSPReply	; dispose of reply bufferjustOpenWindow	jsr AddToPathList	;Add handle to linked list - 16-Mar-93 JCM	clc		rts	***************************************************************** PromptForPassword** Output: CLC if we should try mounting again*****************************************************************PromptForPassword	name	jsr OpenMyResFork	bcc @cont	brl @exit@cont	jsr GetStatus	; 24-Oct-91 MSD	bcs @toerror	; couldn't find server???		pha	pha	;space for NewWindow2	ldx #0	phx	phx	;title	phx	phx	;refcon	phx	phx	;content draw	phx	phx	;defproc	pea 2	;ref is resource	pushlong #1	;ID=1	pea $800E	;rWindParam1	_NewWindow2	plx	ply	stx pwWindow	sty pwWindow+2	bcc @1@toerror	brl @error@1	_InitCursor*** Added 2-Mar-93 JCM - Let's be nice to those that attempt to use us in 320 mode by actually***	     sticking the window fully on the screen.	pha	_GetMasterSCB	pla	and #mode640	bne @showIt	;we're in 640 mode and the window is in a fine location		PushWord #8	;horz	PushWord #34	;vert	PushLong pwWindow	;window to move	_MoveWindow@showIt	PushLong pwWindow	_ShowWindow*** End - 2-Mar-93 JCM	pha	PushWord #$0100	;activate/deactivate events only	pushlong #myEvent	_GetNextEvent	pla		pha	pha	PushWord #15	;tableNum	PushLong #0	;tablePtr	PushWord #$C000	;flags (use 640 colors/don't call CtlNewRes)	ldx #$1612	jsl $E10000;	_UseColorTable	;leave handle on stack	pha	pha	_GetPort	pha	pha	_GetCtlParamPtr	jsr pushPWwindow	_SetPort	pushlong #mySubstitutions	_SetCtlParamPtr; Begin 24-Oct-91 MSD: If no guest access, dim the Guest button and; force the Registered User button on.	lda allowsGuest	; are guests allowed?	bne @guestOK;	pea $00FF	; part code = inactive;	lda #0;	pha	; room for control handle;	pha;	pha	; window (0=FrontWindow);	pha;	pha	; high word of control ID;	pea 5	; Guest control ID;	_GetCtlHandleFromID;	_HiliteControl	; dim the Guest button*** 15-Jul-92 DAL -- use new HiliteCtlByID call	pea $00FF	; inactive	lda #0	pha	pha	;window = NIL	pha	pea 5	;CtlID = Guest radio button	ldx #$3f10	jsl $e10000;	_HiliteCtlByID	;dim the Guest button*** end 15-Jul-92	ldx #4	; Registered User control ID	bra @setGuest	; force Registered User@guestOK; End 24-Oct-91 MSD	ldx #5	;Guest control ID	lda UserName	and #$00ff	beq @setGuest	dex	;4=Registered User control ID@setGuest	phx;	pea 1	;value for SetCtlValue;	pha;	pha	;space for GetCtlHandleFromID result;	pea 0;	pea 0	;window ptr;	pea 0	;high word of ID;	phx	;low word of ID;	_GetCtlHandleFromID;	_SetCtlValue*** 15-Jul-92 DAL -- select radio button, ID in X	pea 1	;value = 1	lda #0	pha	pha	;window = NIL	pha	phx	;ctlID = X	ldx #$3c10	jsl $e10000;	_SetCtlValueByID*** end 15-Jul-92	plx	cpx #5	;guest	bne @notGuest	jsr hitGuest@notGuest	ldx #6@fetchPW	lda Password,x	sta pwBuffer+1,x	dex	dex	bpl @fetchPW	sep #$20	ldx #9	;17-Mar-93 JCM (was 8) - allows 8-char passwords@getPWlen	dex	beq @end	lda pwBuffer,x	beq @getPWlen@end	txa	sta pwBuffer		rep #$30	jsr pushPWwindow	pea 0	pea 6	;password editline	pushlong #pwBuffer	_SetLETextByID	jsr pushPWwindow	pea 0	pea 7	;username editline	pushlong #Username	_SetLETextByID	stz CancelFlag@modal	pha	pha	;space for DoModalWindow	pushlong #myEvent	ldx #0	phx	phx	;update routine	pea $8000	;handle Apple-period	phx	;event hook	phx	phx	;beep proc	pea $4019	;flags (17-Jul-92 DAL)	_DoModalWindow	pla	plx	asl a	cmp #hitTableEnd-hitTable	bcs @modal	tax	jsr (hitTable,x)	bcc @modal	_SetCtlParamPtr	_SetPort	jsr pushPWwindow	_CloseWindow	PushWord #$4000	;flags (don't call CtlNewRes)	ldx #$1712	jsl $E10000;	_RestoreColorTable	_InitCursor	lda CancelFlag	cmp #1	;sec if nonzero	bra @okay@error	jsr ShowErrorWindow@okay	php	jsr CloseMyResFork	plp@exit	rtspushPWwindow	name	plx	pushlong pwWindow	phx	rtspwWindow	dc.l 0CancelFlag	dc.w 0mySubstitutions	dc.l EntityName	; *0 = server namemyEvent	ds.b 46hitTable	dc.w hitIgnore	;0	dc.w hitSave	;1	dc.w hitCancel	;2	dc.w hitConnect	;3	dc.w hitRegistered	;4	dc.w hitGuest	;5hitTableEndhitIgnore	name	clc	rtshitSave	name	jsr ExtractInfo	ldx theFilePath+2	lda theFilePath	jsr RewriteAliasFile	bcc @ok	jsr ShowErrorWindow@ok	clc	rtshitCancel	name	inc CancelFlag	sec	rtshitConnect	name	jsr ExtractInfo	sec	rts** ExtractInfo -- suck info out of dialog controls into ReadBuffer*ExtractInfo	name	stz UserName	stz Password	stz Password+2	stz Password+4	stz Password+6	pha	;space for result	jsr pushPWwindow	pea 1	;family number	_FindRadioButton	pla	bne @guest	jsr pushPWwindow	pea 0	pea 6	;password editline	pushlong #pwBuffer	_GetLETextByID	sep #$30	ldy pwBuffer	beq @done@copypw	lda pwBuffer,y	sta Password-1,y	dey	bne @copypw@done	rep #$30	jsr pushPWwindow	pea 0	pea 7	;username editline	pushlong #UserName	_GetLETextByID@guest	rts** Hit on Guest radio button -- hide name and password items*hitGuest	name	lda #6	jsr HideControlA	lda #7	jsr HideControlA	lda #$A	jsr HideControlA	lda #$B	jsr HideControlA	clc	rtshitRegistered	name	lda #6	jsr ShowControlA	lda #7	jsr ShowControlA	lda #$A	jsr ShowControlA	lda #$B	jsr ShowControlA	clc	rtsHideControlA	name	pha	pha	;space for GetCtlHandleFromID	pea 0	pea 0	;window	pea 0	;high word of ctl id	pha	;low word of ctl id	_GetCtlHandleFromID	_EraseControl	rtsShowControlA	name	pha	pha	;space for GetCtlHandleFromID	pea 0	pea 0	;window	pea 0	;high word of ctl id	pha	;low word of ctl id	_GetCtlHandleFromID	_ShowControl	rts	pwBuffer	ds.b 10	;8 + length byte + terminating zero***************************************************************** OpenMyResFork****************************************************************OpenMyResFork	name;	pha;	_GetCurResourceApp;	pla;	sta oldResApp;;	lda myMemID;	pha;	_ResourceStartUp;;	pha	;space for OpenResourceFile;	pea 1	;read only;	pea 0;	pea 0	;map ptr = NIL;	pha;	pha	;space for LGetPathname2;	lda myMemID;	pha;	pea 1;	_LGetPathname2;	_OpenResourceFile;	plx*** 15-Jul-92 DAL -- saved 39 bytes by using OpenResourceFileByID	pha	;space for old ResApp	pea 0	;requested access	lda myMemID	pha	;my user ID	ldx #$2E1E	jsl $e10000;	_OpenResourceFileByID	pla	sta oldResApp*** end 15-Jul-92	rts	;return CLC=okay***************************************************************** CloseMyResFork****************************************************************CloseMyResFork	name	_ResourceShutDown	lda oldResApp	pha	_SetCurResourceApp	rtsoldResApp	dc.w 0***************************************************************** ReadData -- with file name in XY, read image of QuickMount*             document into ReadBuffer.  Also adds a handle*             to the linked list with the pathname to be*             opened or launched.****************************************************************ReadData	NAMEreadFileTempPtr	equ 1	phd	pha	;readFileTempPtr	pha		tsc	tcd	stx FileNamePtr+2	sty FileNamePtr	stz AliasPCount	;Clear flag for old format		lda #1	sta OpenAccess	_OpenGS OpenBlock	;open up this EasyMount document	bcs @exitReadData		lda OpenRef	sta ReadRef	sta ReadPathRef	sta CloseRef	_ReadGS ReadBlock	;read the standard header, plus 2 bytes	bcs @exitCloseFile	; (so we can check if it's an old file)*** Added - 2-Mar-93 JCM - Again, when the Control key is down during the opening of***	       an alias, we don't open the window that is the target of the***	       alias.	lda theModifiers	and #$1000	;control key?	beq @parseIt		clc	lda #0		bra @exitCloseFile*** End - 2-Mar-93 JCM@parseIt	lda #$FFFF	;flag = file is on disk	jsr ParseFile@exitCloseFile	php	pha	_CloseGS CloseBlock	;@ItsAServer	pla	plp@exitReadData	ply	;actually preserve any error code	ply		pld	rtsdisposePathHandle	NAME	lda PathHandle+2	;Release the handle containing the path	pha	lda PathHandle	pha	_DisposeHandle	rts			*************************************************************************************************** ParseFile - This function examines the EasyMount document data stored at ReadBuffer, and*             builds a pathname (in a new handle) to the file the alias references. All errors*             are returned in the Accumulator, with the carry bit indicating the validity of*             the error.**             This function handle both EasyMount 1.0 documents (a.k.a. QuickMount documents)*             and EasyMount 1.1 files, of which it can create the latter. The new document*             format supports a limited aliasing mechanism to non-server entities.*ParseFile	NAME	sta @onDiskFlag	;true if document is really from disk, not an srqMountServer call	lda AliasPCount	;Check for old style EasyMount document	bne @parseNewStyle		brl @parseOldStyle	; OK, it's not an old style EM document.  This means there a variable sized ; pathname tacked on to the end of the file which we need to load.  We'll create; a handle of the appropriate size, lock it, and read the pathname into it.@parseNewStyle	pha	;Space for result	pha	pea 0	;Push size for path handle	lda AliasPathSize		sta ReadPathLen	;Store for read as well	clc	adc #6	;Plus space for length word	pha	; and linked list handle.	lda myMemID	;Memory ID	pha	pea $8000	;Locked	lda #0	pha	pha	_NewHandle	ply	sty PathHandle	sty <readFileTempPtr	plx	stx PathHandle+2	stx <readFileTempPtr+2	bcs @exitNewStyle	ldy #2	;get a ptr to the new path handle	lda [<readFileTempPtr],y	tax	lda [<readFileTempPtr]	clc	adc #6	bcc @getThePath		inx	@getThePath	sta PathPtr	stx PathPtr+2	lda @onDiskFlag	;is this from srqMountServer?	bne @readDiskPath	; nope, it's really a disk file	ldy ReadPathPtr+2	phy	ldy ReadPathPtr	phy	;source path ptr	phx	pha	;dest ptr to new handle block	pea 0	lda AliasPathSize	pha	_BlockMove	bra @savePathLength@readDiskPath	jsr ReadAliasPathname	bcs @exitNewStyle	;bad read@savePathLength	ldy #2	;get a fresh ptr to the new path handle	lda [<readFileTempPtr],y	tax	lda [<readFileTempPtr]	sta <readFileTempPtr	stx <readFileTempPtr+2	iny	iny	lda AliasPathSize	;Save length word	sta [<readFileTempPtr],y	@exitNewStyle	rts; It's an old style EasyMount document.  This means it doesn't have a pathname; attached to the end so we need to generate one from the volume name by; adding a leading colon and creating a new handle.@parseOldStyle	pha	pha	pea 0	lda VolumeName	;Get size	and #$00ff	clc	adc #7	;Plus length word, linked list	pha	; handle, and leading colon	lda myMemID	pha	pea $8000	lda #0	pha	pha	_NewHandle	ply	sty PathHandle	sty <readFileTempPtr	plx	stx PathHandle+2	stx <readFileTempPtr+2	bcs @exitOldStyle		ldy #2	;Get a ptr to the path handle	lda [<readFileTempPtr],y	tax	lda [<readFileTempPtr]	sta <readFileTempPtr	stx <readFileTempPtr+2		pea volumeName+1>>16 ;Push src address	pea volumeName+1	clc	adc #7	bcc @5	inx@5	phx	;Push dest address	pha		lda volumeName	;Push length including length byte	and #$00ff	pea 0	pha	_BlockMove	;	lda #0	;Clear linked list field;	sta [<readFileTempPtr];	ldy #2;	sta [<readFileTempPtr],y	lda VolumeName	;Fix length word	and #$00ff	inc a	;Account for extra colon	sta FullPathLen	stz FullPathLen+2	;length of the real file we're attaching to this alias;	iny;	iny	ldy #4	sta [<readFileTempPtr],y		iny	iny	sep #$20	;Insert the leading colon	longa off	lda #':'	sta [<readFileTempPtr],y	rep #$20	longa on	clc	;everything went fine	@exitOldStyle	rts@onDiskFlag	DS.W 1********************************************************************************************* ReadAliasPathname - This is used to read the pathname of the file the alias references.*                     The path is at the end of EasyMount 1.1 documents.*ReadAliasPathname	NAME	lda PathPtr+2	sta ReadPathPtr+2	lda PathPtr	sta ReadPathPtr	_ReadGS ReadPathBlock	bcs @exitBadRead		rts@exitBadRead	php	pha	jsr disposePathHandle ;clean up after ourselves	pla	plp	rts***************************************************************** ExtractPathPtr -- Sets pathPtr and pathHandle to the first*	item of the linked list and removes that*	item from the list.  PathHandle is returned*	locked.****************************************************************ExtractPathPtr	name@tempHandle	equ 1@tempPathPtr	equ 5	phd	pha	;tempHandle	pha		pha	;tempPathPtr	pha		tsc	tcd	lda PathListHandle	;Get handle of first item	sta @tempHandle	sta PathHandle	lda PathListHandle+2	sta @tempHandle+2	sta PathHandle+2	pha	;Push for _HLock	pei @tempHandle	_HLock	;Lock while we have a ptr to it		ldy #2	;Get ptr to first item	lda [<@tempHandle]	sta @tempPathPtr	sta PathPtr	lda [<@tempHandle],y	sta @tempPathPtr+2	sta PathPtr+2		lda [<@tempPathPtr]	;Change pathListHandle to point	sta PathListHandle	;to next item in list.	lda [<@tempPathPtr],y	sta PathListHandle+2		clc	;Move ptr past linked handle	lda PathPtr	adc #4	sta PathPtr	bcc @Done	inc PathPtr+2	@Done	pla	pla		pla	pla		pld	rts***************************************************************** AddToPathList --  Appends the handle in PathHandle to the end*	of our linked list.****************************************************************AddToPathList	name@tempHandle	equ 1@tempPathPtr	equ 5		lda theModifiers	and #$1000	;control key?	bne @doneAdd	phd	pha	;tempHandle	pha		pha	;tempPathPtr	pha		tsc	tcd	lda PathHandle+2	;get a local copy of the PathHandle to play with	pha	;for unlock below	sta @tempHandle+2	lda PathHandle	pha	;for unlock below	sta @tempHandle		ldy #2	;dereference PathHandle	lda [<@tempHandle]	sta @tempPathPtr	lda [<@tempHandle],y	sta @tempPathPtr+2		lda PathListHandle	;link the old PathListHandle to the new path 	sta [<@tempPathPtr] ; - this makes the new path the first in the list	lda PathListHandle+2	sta [<@tempPathPtr],y		lda PathHandle+2	;save the new path as the new head of the linked-list	sta PathListHandle+2	lda PathHandle	sta PathListHandle		_HUnlock	;It can be unlocked until we need it at idle time	pla	pla		pla	pla			pld	@doneAdd	rts******************************************************************************************************************************OpenBlock	dc.w 3		;PCountOpenRef	dc.w 0FileNamePtr	ds.l 1OpenAccess	dc.w 1		;Read onlyReadBlock	dc.w 4		;PCountReadRef	dc.w 0	dc.l ReadBuffer	dc.l ReadBufferLen	dc.l 0ReadPathBlock	dc.w 4ReadPathRef	dc.w 0ReadPathPtr	dc.l 0ReadPathLen	dc.l 0	dc.l 0	FullPathBlock	dc.w 4	;Fields filled in manuallyFullPathRef	dc.w 0FullPathPtr	dc.l 0FullPathLen	dc.l 0	dc.l 0	CloseBlock	dc.w 1		;PCountCloseRef	dc.w 0theFilePath	dc.l 0	;pathname ptr used for reading and writing alias file** ReadBuffer is an image of a QuickMount document*theDataLength	dc.w 0	;space for size of ReadBuffer data (for SendRequest(srqMountVolume))ReadBufferEntityName	ds.b 32	;servername + AFPServer + zone, crammed together	ds.b 32	ds.b 33VolumeName	ds.b 28UserName	ds.b 32Password	ds.b 8VPassword	ds.b 8AliasPCount	ds.w 1	;New format, this value is zero if theAliasPathSize	ds.w 1	;document is for a server, 1 otherwise.EndOfReadBufReadBufferLen	equ EndOfReadBuf-ReadBuffer-1PathHandle	ds.l 1PathListHandle	dc.l 0PathPtr	ds.l 1ZeroReadBuffer	name	ldx #ReadBufferLen-2@zero	stz ReadBuffer,x	dex	bpl @zero	rtsTryMountError	dc.w 0ATKerrors	dc.w $400		;Err1	dc.w $401		;Err2	dc.w $404		;Err2	dc.w $406		;Err3	dc.w $408		;Err4	dc.w $a01		;Err5	dc.w $a02		;Err6	dc.w $a03		;Err7;	dc.w $a13		;Err8	dc.w $a15		;Err9	dc.w $a16		;Err10	dc.w $a17		;Err11	dc.w $a18		;Err12	dc.w $a19		;Err13	dc.w $a05		;Err14	dc.w $a06		;Err15	dc.w $a09		;Err15	dc.w $a07		;Err16	dc.w $a08		;Err17	dc.w $a11		;Err18ETable	dc.w Err1	dc.w Err2	dc.w Err2	dc.w Err3	dc.w Err4	dc.w Err5	dc.w Err6	dc.w Err7;	dc.w Err8	dc.w Err9	dc.w Err10	dc.w Err11	dc.w Err12	dc.w Err13	dc.w Err14	dc.w Err15	dc.w Err15	dc.w Err16	dc.w Err17	dc.w Err18	dc.w Err19	;generic error (must be last);Err1	dc.b '62~The volume Ò*0Ó could not be mounted because the server was ';	dc.b 'not found.  Check the zone and server name.~^#0',0Err1	dc.b '62~The shared disk Ò*0Ó could not be found on the network.~^#0',0	;25-Mar-92 DALErr2	dc.b '62~More than one server found.~^#0',0Err3	dc.b '62~Invalid server/zone name.~^#0',0Err4	dc.b '62~AppleTalk is busy or not installed.  (Try closing any open network control panels.)~^#0',0Err5	dc.b '62~There are too many AppleTalk sessions.~^#0',0Err6	dc.b '62~Unable to open session with server.~^#0',0Err7	dc.b '62~The server is not responding.~^#0',0;;;Err9	dc.b '62~You are not authorized to use this server.  Check your password.~^#0',0Err9	dc.b '62~Sorry, your password is incorrect.  Please reenter it.~^#0',0	;15-Sep-92 DALErr10	dc.b '62~Unknown user name for this server.~^#0',0Err11	dc.b '62~The server is shutting down (or maybe starting up), so you canÕt log on now.~^#0',0Err12	dc.b '62~This file server does not use a recognizable log on sequence.~^#0',0Err13	dc.b '62~The server does not support AppleShare 2.0.~^#0',0Err14	dc.b '62~Invalid disk name.~^#0',0			;25-Mar-92 DALErr15	dc.b '62~Unknown disk name.~^#0',0			;25-Mar-92 DALErr16	dc.b '62~You are not authorized to use this shared disk.~^#0',0	;25-Mar-92 DALErr17	dc.b '62~The shared disk could not be made available, because you are using too many '	dc.b 'shared disks at once.~^#0',0			;25-Mar-92 DALErr18	dc.b '62~This shared disk is already available.~^#0',0		;25-Mar-92 DALErr19	dc.b '62~An unknown error occured.  ($*1)~^#0',0 ;must be last string in table!ErrNope	dc.b '53~You can make aliases for disks, folders, and applications only.~^#6',0	;25-Mar-93 JCMKillBlock	dc.b $00	;Synchronous	dc.b $46	;NBPKill	dc.w 0	dc.l LookupBlockLookupBlock	dc.b $00	;Synchronous (24-Oct-91 MSD, was async)	dc.b $10	;LookupLookupResult	dc.w 0	;Result	dc.l 0	;Completion routine	dc.l EntityName	;Entity name pointerLookupT	dc.b 1	;1/4 second	dc.b 20	;20 times	dc.w 0	;Reserved	dc.w LUpBufferLen	;Buffer length	dc.l LUpBuffer	;Buffer pointer	dc.b 1	;Max # matchesLookupCount	dc.b 0	;Actual matchesLUpBufferLUpNet	dc.w 0LUpNodeSocket	dc.w 0	dc.b 0		;Enumerator	ds.b 32	ds.b 32	ds.b 33LUpBufferLen	equ *-LUpBufferGetMyZoneBlock	dc.b $00		;Synchronous	dc.b $A		;GetMyZone	dc.w 0	dc.l 0MyZonePtr	dc.l 0	dc.b 2	dc.b 2	dc.w 0Login2Block	dc.b $00		;Synchronous	dc.b $38		;Login2LoginResult	dc.w 0		;ResultLoginNet	dc.w 0LoginNodeSocket	dc.w 0CmdBLen	dc.w CmdBaseLenCmdBufferPtr	dc.l CmdBuffer	dc.w RplyBufferLen	dc.l RplyBufferLoginSession	dc.b 0	dc.l 0	dc.l EntityNameLoginZone	dc.l EntityName	dc.w $0200		;AFP version wordLoginCBlock	dc.b $00		;Synchronous	dc.b $2C		;LoginCont	dc.w 0		;ResultLoginCSession	dc.b 0	dc.w Cmd2BufferLen	dc.l Cmd2Buffer	dc.w RplyBufferLen	dc.l RplyBufferDESBlock	dc.l Password	dc.l RplyRndm	dc.l Cmd2RandomCmdBuffer	dc.b 18	str 'AFPVersion 2.0'	str 'Randnum exchange'CmdBaseLen	equ *-CmdBufferCmdUser	ds.b 32GuestLogin	dc.b 18	str 'AFPVersion 2.0'GuestUAM	str 'No User Authent'GuestLoginLen	equ *-GuestLoginCmd2Buffer	dc.b 19	dc.b 0Cmd2ID	dc.w 0		;ID numberCmd2Random	dcb.b 8,0		;Random number exchangeCmd2BufferLen	equ *-Cmd2BufferRplyBufferRplyID	dc.w 0RplyRndm	dcb.b 8,0RplyBufferLen	equ *-RplyBufferMountVolBlock	dc.b $00		;Synchronous	dc.b $2E		;MountVol	dc.w 0		;ResultMountSession	dc.b 0MountVolFlags	dc.b $C0	dc.l VolumeName	dc.w 0		;Vol ID	dc.b 0		;Slot/Drive	dc.l VPasswordLogoutBlock	dc.b $00		;Synchronous	dc.b $2D		;FILogout	dc.w 0		;ResultLogoutSession	dc.b 0CAFPName	str 'AFPServer'; Added the following variables 24-Oct-91 MSDSPReplyLen	equ 2048	; more than enough!SPReplyHandle	dc.l 0	; handle to ASP reply bufferSPCommand	dc.b $00,$20	; sync SPCommand	dc.w 0	; result	dc.l 0	; completion routineSPCmdSession	dc.b 0	; session refnum	dc.w GetSrvrParmsLen ; command block length	dc.l FPGetSrvrParms	; command block pointer	dc.w SPReplyLen	; reply buffer length	dc.l 0	; reply buffer pointer	dc.l 0	; AFP command result	dc.w 0	; actual reply lengthFPGetSrvrParms	dc.b $10	; GetSrvrParms command numberGetSrvrParmsLen	equ *-FPGetSrvrParmsSPGetStatus	dc.b $00,$1D	; sync SPGetStatus	dc.w 0	dc.l 0	dc.l 0	; server internet address	dc.w SPReplyLen	dc.l 0	; pointer to reply buffer	dc.l 0	; AFP result	dc.w 0	; actual reply lengthallowsGuest	dc.w 0	; non-zero if Guest access allowed; End 24-Oct-91 MSD; Added 8-Nov-91 MSDGetUserPath	dc.w 3	; pcount	dc.w $D	; AppleShare FST	dc.w 8	; GetUserPath call	dc.l 0	; path pointer returned here; End 8-Nov-91 MSD;-----------------------------------------------------------------------------------;; 3-Nov-91 MSD: Separated the Lookup code so it can be called just once before any; other routines use the address.;FindServer	name	ldx #LookupBlock	ldy #^LookupBlock	jsl >RamDispatch	lda LookupBlock+2	; get result	bcs @exit		lda LookupCount	; get number of servers found	and #$00FF	; just a byte	dea	; if 1, leave 0 in A	beq @exit	; one found, return carry clear		sec	; no server found	lda #$0400	; fake no server found error@exit	rts	; return with carry set if error;; 29-Oct-91 MSD: Added TestLoggedOn so that if the Option key is down, we can; decide not to show the dialog box if we're already logged on.  Returns with; carry set if we're already logged on to the server.;TestLoggedOn	name	lda LUpNet	sta LoginNet	lda LUpNodeSocket	sta LoginNodeSocket	stz CmdBLen	; don't actually log on, just test it		ldx #Login2Block	ldy #^Login2Block	jsl >RamDispatch@exit	rts	; return carry set if logged on; End 29-Oct-91******************************************************************************** TryMount** Calls TryMount2 and handles volume-already-mounted by asking the Finder* to open the window.** (If the Control key is down, we don't try.)*******************************************************************************TryMount	name		jsr TryMount2	bcc @openIt	cmp #$0a11	;volume already mounted?	beq @openIt	sec	rts@openIt	*** added 18-Nov-91 DAL -- force Finder to schedule mounting this volume	pha	_ScanDevices	;force Finder's notify proc to see this insert	pla*** end 18-Nov-91 DAL	stz TryMountError	clc	rtsopenWindowOut	dc.w 0	;receive count	dc.w 0	;finder result	dc.l 0	;window pointerhandleFinderIdle	name* If our linked list of pathnames to open is nil, then we have nothing pending to open.	lda PathListHandle+1 ;is the list empty?	bne @HandleAction	; nope, open up one more	brl @NoAction	; yup, just exit; Save system prefs for restore after GetFileInfo@HandleAction	_GetSysPrefsGS SavePrefBlock	;Set System prefs temporarily to make sure we prompt for offline volumes.	_SetSysPrefsGS MyPrefBlock		jsr ExtractPathPtr	;Set up ptr and handle to pathname	lda PathPtr	ldy PathPtr+2	jsr GetFileInfo	pha	;Restore preferences	_SetSysPrefsGS SavePrefBlock		pla	;Restore error code from GetFileInfo	beq @NoError	cmp #$40	;If bad path syntax, assume it's	beq @DoOpenWindow	;something we want to openWindow on	brl @CleanUpPending	;Other errors, exit.;A volume was requested that was offline.  @NoError		*** Added - 25-Mar-93 JCM - If it's a folder or disk, open the window, if it's an app, launch it.***	         Otherwise, we ignore it.	jsr ValidateType		bcs @NoAction		cmp #$0f	beq @DoOpenWindow	bra @DoOpenApp	;must be an application;	ldy MyFileInfoType	;Is it a folder?;	cpy #$0f;	beq @DoOpenWindow;	;	cpy #$ff	;Try application;	beq @DoOpenApp;	;	cpy #$b3;	beq @DoOpenApp;	;	cpy #$b5;	beq @DoOpenApp;;	bra @DoOpenDoc	;Default to document*** End - 25-Mar-93 JCM@NoAction	clc	rts@DoOpenApp	lda PathPtr	;Set up pathname to launch	ldy PathPtr+2	sta LaunchPathPtr	sty LaunchPathPtr+2	stz LaunchBlock		pea tellFinderLaunchThis	pea sendToName+stopAfterOne	pushlong #nameOfFinder	pushlong #LaunchBlock	bra @FinishSendReq;@DoOpenDoc	bra @CleanUpPending	;Need to add this! - 25-Mar-93 JCM - removed for now@DoOpenWindow	pea tellFinderOpenWindow	pea sendToName+stopAfterOne	pushlong #nameOfFinder	pushlong PathPtr@FinishSendReq	pushlong #openWindowOut	_SendRequest@CleanUpPending	jsr disposePathHandle@Done	sec	rts*** Added - 25-Mar-93 JCMGetFileInfo	sta FileInfoPathPtr	sty FileInfoPathPtr+2	_GetFileInfoGS FileInfoBlock	rtsValidateType	lda MyFileInfoType	;Is it a folder?	cmp #$0f	beq @typeOk		cmp #$ff	;Try application	beq @typeOk		cmp #$b3	beq @typeOk		cmp #$b5	beq @typeOk@typeBad	sec	rts@typeOk	clc		rts*** End - 25-Mar-93 JCMTempEvent	ds.b 16LaunchBlock	dc.w 0LaunchPathPtr	ds.l 1FileInfoBlock	dc.w 3FileInfoPathPtr	ds.l 1	ds.w 1MyFileInfoType	ds.w 1SavePrefBlock	dc.w 1	dc.w 0	MyPrefBlock	dc.w 1	;Allow volume mount dialog	dc.w %1000000000000000	*** added 8-Jan-92 DAL -- If our device gets ejected, don't try to open it*** (This is important in case we mount something that turns out to be a*** duplicate-named volume.  We can't necessarily tell in advance.)***handleEjectingDev	lda PathListHandle+1	bne @pending	@reject	clc	;reject event, nothing pending		rts@pending	sec	;accept the systemSaysEjectingDev event		rts*** end 8-Jan-92******************************************************************************** TryMount2** Inputs: EntityName, VolumeName, UserName, Password, VPassword** Outputs:  network error code in A and TryMountError (SEC if error)*******************************************************************************; 24-Oct-91 MSD: Changed the lookup to be synchronous, removed the checking for; the call to complete and the NBPKill call.TryMount2	name	stz TryMountError	; assume no error	lda LUpNet	sta LoginNet	lda LUpNodeSocket	sta LoginNodeSocket	lda UserName	;is there a user name?	and #$00ff	beq doGuest	;no, login as guest	lda #CmdBuffer	;set pointer to correct login block	sta CmdBufferPtr	lda #^CmdBuffer	sta CmdBufferPtr+2	sep #$30	longa off	longi off	ldx UserNameUNLoop	lda UserName,x	sta CmdUser,x	dex	bpl UNLoop	rep #$30	longa on	longi on	lda UserName	and #$00FF	sec	adc #CmdBaseLen	sta CmdBLen	bra skipGuestdoGuest	lda #GuestLogin	sta CmdBufferPtr	lda #^GuestLogin	sta CmdBufferPtr+2	lda #GuestLoginLen	sta CmdBLenskipGuest	lda EntityName	;initialize zone name pointer in command	and #$00ff	;block to point to zone name within	inc a	;entity name.	tay	sec	adc EntityName,y	and #$00ff	clc	adc #EntityName	sta LoginZone	lda #^EntityName	sta LoginZone+2	ldx #Login2Block	ldy #^Login2Block	jsl >RamDispatch	sep #$30	lda LoginSession	sta LoginCSession	sta MountSession	sta LogoutSession	sta SPCmdSession	; Added 24-Oct-91 MSD	rep #$30	bcc L2	lda LoginResult	cmp #$0A04	; login continue (want password)	beq L3	cmp #$0A13	; already logged on	beq L2BadExit	sec	sta TryMountError	rtsL3	lda RplyID	sta Cmd2ID*** DES needs <0..<7 on direct page	phd	pha	pha	pha	pha	tsc	inc a	tcd	ldx #DESBlock	ldy #^DESBlock	jsl DES	pla	pla	pla	pla	pld*** unfutz direct page	ldx #LoginCBlock	ldy #^LoginCBlock	jsl >RamDispatch	lda LoginCBlock+2	bcs BadExitL2	jsr TestUserVolume	; see if User Volume bit should be set	bcs @logoff	; couldn't find volume name!	ldx #MountVolBlock	ldy #^MountVolBlock	jsl >RamDispatch	bcc @L2	lda MountVolBlock+2	sta TryMountError	cmp #$0A11	; was volume already mounted?	beq @L2	;The carry will be set!;; 24-Oct-91 MSD: We couldn't mount the volume.  If we were already; logged on, don't bother logging off.;@logoff	ldx LoginResult	cpx #$0A13	; FILogin2 get already logged in error?	beq @L2	; Yes, don't log off (note: carry will be set!); End 24-Oct-91 MSD	pha	; save error code	ldx #LogoutBlock	ldy #^LogoutBlock	jsl >RamDispatch	pla	; recover error code	sec@L2	rts;; 24-Oct-91 MSD: Do an SPGetStatus to see if the server supports guest access; (the "No User Authent" string will be in the list of UAMs).  Set allowsGuest; to a non-zero value if guests are allowed.;GetStatus	name; Make a stack frame for local variables.  They are:; 1,s  Pointer into reply buffer; 5,s  Count of UAM strings	phd	pha	pha	pha	tsc	tcd		stz allowsGuest	; assume no guest access; Copy pointer to ASP reply buffer to direct page	lda SPGetStatus+$E	sta <1	lda SPGetStatus+$10	sta <3		lda LUpNet	; copy server's address	sta SPGetStatus+8	lda LUpNodeSocket	sta SPGetStatus+10@retry	ldx #<SPGetStatus	ldy #^SPGetStatus	jsl >RamDispatch	; get info from server	lda SPGetStatus+2	bcc @gotstat	cmp #$0702	; is ASP busy?	beq @retry	; yes, so try call again	sec	; return error	bra @exit@gotstat	ldy #4	lda [1],y	; get offset to count of UAM's	xba	; put in 65816 order	tay	lda [1],y	; get count of number of UAM's	and #$00FF	; just a byte	sta <5	; save count	tya	; get offset to UAM count byte	sec	; add one for count byte	adc <1	; point to first UAM string	sta <1; For each UAM string, compare it to the Guest UAM@loop	pha	; result of compare	pea $0000	; flags (reserved)	pei <3	; push pointer to this UAM string	pei <1	pushlong #GuestUAM	; point to the Guest UAM string	_CompareStrings	pla	beq @match	; equal, so set flag		lda [1]	; get string length	and #$00FF	; just a byte	sec	; add one for length byte	adc <1	sta <1	; point to next UAM string		dec <5	; more to check?	bne @loop	beq @noerr	; no, so leave it alone@match	inc allowsGuest	; set the flag@noerr	clc	; no error@exit	ply	; clean up stack	ply	ply	pld		rts; End 24-Oct-91 MSD;; 24-Oct-91 MSD: Do an FPGetSrvrParms and find the volume in the list to see; if it is a user volume (i.e., the hasConfigInfo bit is set); we'll also know; if the volume has a volume password (as if anybody cares).  If for any reason; we can't find the volume, leave the user volume bit clear.;TestUserVolume	name;; Make a stack frame for some local variables.  They are:; 1,s  Pointer into reply buffer; 5,s  Number of volumes left to check;	phd	pha	; create room for some direct page variables	pha	pha	tsc	tcd	; make local stack frame		lda MountVolFlags	and #$FFFE	; clear user volume bit by default	sta MountVolFlags; Copy pointer to ASP reply buffer to direct page	lda SPCommand+$11	sta <1	lda SPCommand+$13	sta <3	; Attempt the FPGetSrvrParms (retry if ASP is busy)@retry	ldx #<SPCommand	ldy #^SPCommand	jsl >RamDispatch	bcc @gotparms	lda SPCommand+2	; get result	cmp #$0702	; is ASP busy (too many calls)?	beq @retry	; if so, keep trying	bne @errexit	; some other error, give up@gotparms; Now see if we can find a matching volume in the list.	ldy #4	; offset to number of volumes in reply	lda [1],y	; get number of volumes	and #$00FF	; just a byte	sta <5	; save for loop	beq @noVolumes	;added 17-Sep-92 DAL	clc	lda <1	adc #6	; point to first volume's length byte	sta <1	; For each volume, compare it to given volume name@loop	pha	; result of compare	pea $0000	; flags (reserved)	pei <3	; push pointer to volume in list	pei <1	pushlong #VolumeName	_CompareStrings	pla	bne @next@match	dec <1	; point to flags before length byte	lda [1]	; get flags	and #$0001	; get only hasConfigInfo flag	ora MountVolFlags	; put into MountVolFlags (same bit)	sta MountVolFlags	clc	; no error	bra @exit	; done!@next	lda [1]	; get length of volume name	and #$00FF	; just one byte	sec	; add 1 for length byte	adc <1	; point to flags for next volume	ina	; point to string length for next volume	sta <1		dec <5	; any more volumes to check?	bne @loop@noVolumes		lda #$0A06	; volume not found!@errexit	sec	; error@exit	ply	; clean up stack frame	ply	ply	pld		rtsAllocSPReply	pha	pha	; room for result (handle)	pushlong #SPReplyLen	lda myMemID	pha	pea $C010	; locked, fixed, no cross bank boundary	pha	; starting location ignored	pha	_NewHandle	; allocate ASP's buffer	plx	ply	bcs @exit		stx SPReplyHandle	sty SPReplyHandle+2		phd	phy	phx	tsc	tcd	ldy #2	lda [1],y	; deref handle	sta SPCommand+$13	; save for SPCommand	sta SPGetStatus+$10	; save for SPGetStatus	tax	; save for return in X	lda [1]	sta SPCommand+$11	sta SPGetStatus+$E	ply	; remove handle from stack	ply	pld		clc	; pointer in A,X (A low)@exit	rtsFreeSPReply	pushlong SPReplyHandle	_DisposeHandle	rts; End 24-Oct-91 MSD************************************************************************************************************************************************************ReportMountError	name	lda TryMountError	beq @quiet	pha	; error code	pushlong #errNum+1	; pointer to string	pea $0004	; length to convert to	_Int2Hex	; build a hex string for *1		_InitCursor	pha	;space for AlertWindow result	pea $0021	;flags (cool button layout + substitute pStrings)	pushlong #subArray	pea Err1>>16	; push high word of error message pointer		lda TryMountError	ldx #(ETable-ATKerrors)-2	;index of last error number in table@lookup	cmp ATKerrors,x	beq @L0		;found it!	dex	dex	bpl @lookup	ldx #(ETable-ATKErrors)	;use default string@L0	lda ETable,x	pha	; push low word of message pointer	_AlertWindow	; show the alert	pla	; ignore the button pressed@quiet	rtssubArray	dc.l VolumeName	; for Err1	dc.l errNum	; for generic errorerrNum	dc.b 4,'0000'	; four-digit hex number******************************************************************************	EndP	End